# Anchored to the repo root on purpose: an unanchored `data/` would also match
# src/taxoquiz/data/, which holds the committed example dataset. That silently
# excluded it from built wheels, since hatchling honours .gitignore.
# data/ is generated and large, so it stays out of git — except this README,
# which explains what all the generated files are. Written as /data/* rather
# than /data/ so git will descend far enough to see the negation below.
/data/*
!/data/README.md
/.venv/
# `python -m build` output. Anchored for the same reason /data/ is: an
# unanchored `dist` would also swallow frontend/dist, which frontend/.gitignore
# already handles on its own terms.
/dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
.claude/
